Z||000000||L.I. Fieros||10-18-2000||04:43 PM||||While out on the road cruising through up-state NY enjoying a beautiful day my internal Fiero alarm went off.  I looked to my right and what did I see....3 Fieros sitting in a small grass field.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  The cars seemed to be abandoned to me because there were no tags on any of them and no building that they seemed to be associated with.  There were two 84 coupes (1 base and 1 SE both manual trans.) and one 87 coupe with T-TOPS and 5-speed trans.  The cars are located on Route 4 somewhere between Hudson Falls and Comstock (sorry I don't remember the exact location).  They are on the East side of the road though, and I do remember a large green barn/building almost oppositte them on the West side called the Green Thumb Nursery (or something like that).  So, maybe someone can research them, and possibly rescue these Fieros.  I live too far away and have no room.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> They all seemed to be basically completely intact and in decent shape despite the fact that they have been sitting a little while.<P>Good Luck,<BR>See ya,<BR>Dave||||reg||4
